## 🔍 What's Causing the Delay

Looking at your code in `EditInvoiceScreen.kt`:

Kotlin

```
LaunchedEffect(Unit) {
    viewModel.navigationEvent.collect { event ->
        when (event) {
            is EditInvoiceViewModel.NavigationEvent.BackToInvoiceDetail -> {
                // Show success notification
                scaffoldState.snackbarHostState.showSnackbar(
                    message = "✅ Invoice saved successfully!",
                    duration = SnackbarDuration.Short
                )
                
                // ⏱️ THIS IS THE DELAY - waiting 1.5 seconds
                delay(1500)
                
                // Navigate back to invoice detail screen
                navController.popBackStack()
            }
            // ...
        }
    }
}
```

**The delay exists because:**

- `delay(1500)` = 1.5 seconds (1500 milliseconds)
- This was designed to let the user **see the success message** before navigating away
- But if Snackbar is already gone, the user just sees a blank screen

## 🎯 The Solution: Reduce or Eliminate the Delay

### **Option 1: Reduce to 500ms (Recommended - Best Balance)**

Kotlin

```
delay(500)  // Just enough time to see the message, then go back
