## **STEP 3: Common Fixes (Choose One)**

### **OPTION A: Development Fix (FASTEST - Wipes Data)**

If you're in **early development** and can lose test data:

Kotlin

```
// In DatabaseModule.kt or where you build Room database
Room.databaseBuilder(context, AppDatabase::class.java, "bizap_database.db")
    .fallbackToDestructiveMigration()  // ← Add this line
    .build()
```

**Effect:** Room will delete and recreate the database on schema mismatch. **Pros:** Fast, avoids manual migration writing **Cons:** Deletes all local data (fine for testing) **Use when:** Early dev, test data only

---

### **OPTION B: Auto Migration (SAFER - Preserves Data)**

If you're **closer to production** and want to keep user data:

Kotlin

```
@Database(
    entities = [CustomerEntity::class, /* ... other entities ... */],
    version = 21,  // ← Increment version
    autoMigrations = [
        AutoMigration(from = 20, to = 21)  // ← Add this
    ]
)
abstract class AppDatabase : RoomDatabase() {
    // ... DAOs ...
}
```

**Effect:** Room auto-generates migration based on schema diff **Pros:** Preserves data, handles simple changes (add column, new table) **Cons:** Only works for non-destructive changes **Use when:** Adding columns, new tables, indices

---

### **OPTION C: Manual Migration (MOST CONTROL - Most Work)**

If auto migration doesn't work or you need custom logic:

Kotlin

```
val MIGRATION_20_21 = object : Migration(20, 21) {
    override fun migrate(database: SupportSQLiteDatabase) {
        // Add missing columns
        database.execSQL("ALTER TABLE customers ADD COLUMN address TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''")
        database.execSQL("ALTER TABLE customers ADD COLUMN notes TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''")
        database.execSQL("ALTER TABLE customers ADD COLUMN createdAt INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT ${System.currentTimeMillis()}")
        
        // Create missing indices
        database.execSQL("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_customers_business ON customers(businessProfileId)")
    }
}

@Database(
    entities = [CustomerEntity::class, /* ... */],
    version = 21,
    migrations = [
        /* ... existing migrations ... */
        MIGRATION_20_21  // ← Register it
    ]
)
abstract class AppDatabase : RoomDatabase() {
    // ... DAOs ...
}
```

