Android WorkManager Requirement:
  All Worker classes MUST have a constructor with this signature:
  
    public WorkerClass(Context context, WorkerParameters params)

Why It's Required:
  WorkManager uses reflection to instantiate workers
  It looks for EXACTLY this constructor signature
  If it doesn't exist → NoSuchMethodException → App crashes

Common Causes:

1. Missing Constructor Entirely
   ❌ class ExchangeRateWorker : Worker {
        // No constructor defined
        override fun doWork() { ... }
      }
   
   ✅ class ExchangeRateWorker(
        context: Context,
        params: WorkerParameters
      ) : Worker(context, params) {
        override fun doWork() { ... }
      }

2. Wrong Constructor Signature
   ❌ class ExchangeRateWorker(context: Context) { ... }
      // Missing WorkerParameters parameter
   
   ✅ class ExchangeRateWorker(
        context: Context,
        params: WorkerParameters  // ← Required
      ) { ... }

3. Constructor Parameters in Wrong Order
   ❌ class ExchangeRateWorker(params: WorkerParameters, context: Context) { ... }
      // Wrong order
   
   ✅ class ExchangeRateWorker(
        context: Context,           // ← First
        params: WorkerParameters    // ← Second
      ) { ... }

4. Not Calling Super Constructor
   ❌ class ExchangeRateWorker(
        context: Context,
        params: WorkerParameters
      ) : CoroutineWorker(context, params) {
        // Missing super call or not extending properly
      }
   
   ✅ class ExchangeRateWorker(
        context: Context,
        params: WorkerParameters
      ) : CoroutineWorker(context, params) {  // ← Extends properly
        override suspend fun doWork(): Result { ... }
      }

