WHY ROOM IS SO STRICT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Room throws this error intentionally:

Reason 1: Data Corruption Prevention
  If schema doesn't match Entity, queries will fail
  Data could be lost or corrupted silently
  Room prevents this by failing loudly

Reason 2: Type Safety
  Entity expects: val amount: Double
  But column is: BIGINT (Integer type)
  Result: Type conversion errors, crashes
  Room prevents this

Reason 3: Null Safety
  Entity expects: val name: String (NOT NULL)
  But column is: nullable TEXT
  Result: App crashes when null is loaded
  Room prevents this

Example of Disaster (if Room didn't check):
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Entity says: val amount: Double     │
│ Database is: INTEGER column         │
│                                     │
│ App tries to load: 3.14             │
│ Gets from DB: 3 (truncated!)        │
│ Result: Math errors, wrong totals   │
│ Silent data corruption              │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘

Room prevents this by validating schema match.

