### 6. Create a Pull Request

Once you've pushed your branch to GitHub, navigate to the repository page and create a pull request. Describe the changes you made and request a review from your team members.

### 7. Review Process

Engage with your peers during the review process. Be open to feedback and ready to make changes based on suggestions.

### 8. Merge Your Changes

Once your pull request is approved, you can merge your changes into the main branch.

### 9. Clean Up

After the merge, delete your feature branch both locally and remotely to keep the repository clean:

bash

```
git branch -d your-feature-branch  # Delete local branch

git push origin --delete your-feature-branch  # Delete remote branch
