When the response is not successful, the interceptor **throws an exception without closing the response body**. This is a classic OkHttp resource leak. Per OkHttp docs: _"Each response body is backed by a limited resource... Failing to close the response body will leak resources."_ The response body must be closed with `response.close()` or `response.body?.close()` before throwing.

